        <p>TUESDAY. ~trisrs °‘,llllclllor Hhe . Roberts (in t chair), Jackson Holmes and T. Locker. %-„snnashers.—Two youths, named Ed- Ofin, c/o Mrs. Makinson, Portland- - }Tarry Highley, 103, Catherine- ' summoned for doing damage at the Wire Ropery Works by breaking '--11r. Browne appeared for the firm, that whilst they did not press for a they hoped the boys would be l'ePrimanded by the Bench. They TaYed at a works close by the Wire 11;9W admitted ;bat at three o'clock in they had sent pieces of " scrap " 'lle windows. There was a danger thle machinery might be damaged, or one in the works would receive an 41.,..."e panes of glass had been put in ho employed the boys.—The Chair- r defendants would be put on pro- it twelve months and would have to • ensts ethn• ' • 1.1 teal Assault.—William Willis, 49, a'le, was ordered to pay 3s. 6d. costs assaulted Peter O'Connor, 13, Lock- -It was stated that the children of were "falling (Mt," and that when It to see O'Connor in regard to the gripped him by the throat.—The 1. Said that a technical assault had atted.</p>
